# API security

The browser is untrusted. Only this process connects to MongoDB. Load `api-security` before changing auth, cookies, queries, or anything that calls the network.

| Risk | Required control |
| --- | --- |
| CSRF | `POST /auth/refresh` and `POST /auth/logout` require an `Origin` in the comma-separated `FRONTEND_ORIGIN` allowlist. Cookie is `HttpOnly`, `Secure`, `SameSite=None`, `Path=/api/v1/auth` |
| XSS | JSON only. Do not build HTML from request data. Error bodies omit stacks |
| SSRF | Do not fetch a URL that came from the request. No `fetch`, axios, or `got` in `src` |
| NoSQL injection | Zod allow-list, then an explicit filter. `escapeRegex` on search. No `$where`. Do not pass `req.body` to `find` |
| Auth | `requireAdmin`. Verify JWT with `algorithms: ["HS256"]`. Store the refresh token as a SHA-256 hash. Unknown emails still run a dummy hash |
| Secrets | `passwordHash`, `tokenHash`, refresh tokens, and access tokens stay out of JSON and logs |
| Abuse | Login rate limit. JSON limit 16 KB. `limit` at most 50 |

Do not add a file upload, an open redirect, or a proxy to a client-supplied URL. Helmet and the CORS origin stay on.
